    <bpmn:process id="W_W301" name="W301. Reason Code &amp; Disposition Master Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New operational exception type identified, audit finding requiring new tracking codes, or periodic code rationalization review
Frequency: ~5–10 new reason codes/year; annual rationalization review
Volume: ~100–150 active reason codes across all domains (inventory, returns, vendor, finance); ~15–20 disposition codes
Owner: Master Data Manager
Participants: VP Store Operations, DC Operations Manager, Finance Controller, AP Supervisor, Loss Prevention Officer, Master Data Analyst
Source: workflow W301 — Reason Code &amp; Disposition Master Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W301_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W301_Lane1" name="Operational Stakeholder">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W301_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W301_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W301_Lane2" name="Master Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W301_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W301_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W301_Lane3" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W301_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W301_Lane4" name="Master Data Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W301_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W301_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W301_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W301_Start6" name="New operational exception type identified, audit finding requiring new tracking codes, or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W301_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W301_Task7" name="Code Request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Code Request: Operational stakeholder (Store Operations, DC, Finance, LP) requests a new reason code or disposition code. Request specifies: code domain (inventory adjustment, return, vendor dispute, AP hold, AR write-off, cycle count variance, damaged goods), code description, disposition action (return to stock, scrap, return to vendor, donate, quarantine, hold for investigation), and GL account mapping for financial impact posting.
Responsible (R): Operational Stakeholder
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W301_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W301_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W301_Task8" name="Rationalization Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Rationalization Review: Master Data Analyst reviews existing codes in the same domain to check for duplication or overlap. If a similar code already exists, the request is redirected to use the existing code. If genuinely new, analyst confirms it fills a gap not covered by current codes. Target: no two codes with the same meaning in the same domain.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W301_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W301_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W301_Task9" name="Financial Impact Mapping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Financial Impact Mapping: Finance Controller reviews the GL account mapping for the new code. Ensures that: (a) the correct expense/revenue account is debited/credited, (b) the correct cost center bears the impact, (c) the code&#x27;s financial treatment is consistent with PFRS and the company&#x27;s accounting policies.
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W301_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W301_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W301_Task10" name="System Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System Configuration: Master Data Analyst configures the reason/disposition code in the ERP, specifying: code value, description, domain, applicable modules (POS, WMS, AP, AR, Inventory), disposition action, GL mapping, and mandatory attachment requirement (e.g., &quot;Damage&quot; codes require photo evidence).
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W301_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W301_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W301_Task11" name="Approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Approval: Master Data Manager approves the new code. Confirms alignment with the overall code structure and no redundancy.
Responsible (R): Master Data Manager
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W301_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W301_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W301_Task12" name="Annual Rationalization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual Rationalization: Annually, Master Data Manager conducts a full rationalization review of all reason/disposition codes. Codes with zero usage in 12 months are flagged for deactivation. Codes that are frequently misused (identified by LP audit) are redesigned or merged. New codes proposed by operational teams are evaluated against the existing structure.
Responsible (R): Master Data Manager
Accountable (A): CFO / COO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W301_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W301_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W301_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W301_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-330 (ensure controlled execution — Extended Masters (PA-29.3).) | - operational: evidence (photos, vendor authorization), enabling fraud or compliance gaps
Owner: Master Data Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W301_Assoc15" sourceRef="W301_Annotation14" targetRef="W301_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
