    <bpmn:process id="W_W303" name="W303. Manufacturer/Brand Master Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New brand/manufacturer onboarding, brand acquisition or licensing, private label brand creation (W129), or brand discontinuation
Frequency: ~10–20 new brands/year; ~5 brand changes/quarter; private label brand creation ~1–2/year
Volume: ~500–800 active brands across all categories; ~300–500 active manufacturers; 2–3 private label brands
Owner: Master Data Manager
Participants: Category Manager, VP Merchandising, Legal Counsel, Master Data Analyst
Source: workflow W303 — Manufacturer/Brand Master Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W303_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W303_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W303_Lane2" name="Master Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W303_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W303_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W303_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W303_Start6" name="New brand/manufacturer onboarding, brand acquisition or licensing, private label brand…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W303_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W303_Task7" name="Brand Request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Brand Request: Category Manager requests creation of a new brand or manufacturer in the master. Request specifies: brand name, manufacturer/parent company, country of origin, associated vendors (one brand may be supplied by multiple vendors), product categories the brand covers, and any licensing/trademark considerations.
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W303_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W303_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W303_Task8" name="Deduplication Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Deduplication Check: Master Data Analyst checks for existing brand records using fuzzy matching (brand name similarity, parent company match). Common duplicates: &quot;3M&quot; vs. &quot;3M Philippines&quot; vs. &quot;Minnesota Mining &amp; Mfg&quot;; &quot;Bosch&quot; vs. &quot;Robert Bosch&quot;. If duplicate found, merges instead of creating new.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W303_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W303_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W303_Task9" name="Vendor-Brand Linkage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor-Brand Linkage: Master Data Analyst links the brand to the authorized vendor(s) in the ERP. This establishes the many-to-many relationship: one brand can have multiple vendors (e.g., regional distributors for the same brand), and one vendor can carry multiple brands. Validates that linked vendors are active (W287).
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W303_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W303_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W303_Task10" name="Private Label Governance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Private Label Governance: For private label brands (W129), VP Merchandising and Legal Counsel review: (a) trademark registration status, (b) packaging compliance (FDA/DTI requirements where applicable), (c) approved factory list (W160 — social compliance audit required), and (d) brand positioning and margin targets. Private label brands require additional governance steps including quality testing (W150) and factory audit (W160).
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W303_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W303_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W303_Task11" name="System Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System Configuration: Master Data Analyst configures the brand/manufacturer in the ERP, specifying: brand code, name, manufacturer, country of origin, active status, and linked categories. For private labels, adds the quality compliance flag (requiring factory audit certification before any SKU can be activated).
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W303_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W303_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W303_Task12" name="Downstream Sync">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Downstream Sync: Brand master is synced to: (a) item master (W252 — brand assignment on each SKU), (b) ecommerce (brand filter/facet and brand landing pages), (c) BI/reporting (brand-level sales, margin, and market share analysis), (d) vendor portal (brand authorization for vendor item submissions).
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W303_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W303_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W303_Task13" name="Annual Brand Performance Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual Brand Performance Review: Annually, Category Manager and Master Data Manager review all active brands. Brands with declining sales, quality issues, or vendor relationship changes are flagged. Inactive brands (zero sales in 12 months) are deactivated. Brand rationalization recommendations are submitted to VP Merchandising.
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Master Data Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W303_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W303_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W303_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W303_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-330 (ensure controlled execution — Extended Masters (PA-29.3).) | - operational: Master Data Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Master Data Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W303_Assoc16" sourceRef="W303_Annotation15" targetRef="W303_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W303_Flow17" sourceRef="W303_Start6" targetRef="W303_Task7" />
